guide.lpsm_mb:desc=Welcome to §uMore Blocks§r! This Add-On adds new variants of blocks.\n
guide.lpsm_mb:blocks.sponge=Sponge
guide.lpsm_mb:blocks.tnt=TNT
guide.lpsm_mb:blocks.redstone_block=Redstone Block
##template: guide.lpsm_mb:blocks.stairs.desc=§lStairs§r are blocks that allow mobs and players to change elevation without jumping.\n\n§lObtained:§r Crafted by placing 6 blocks in a stair like shape.\n\n§lVariants:§r {{stairs}}.\n
guide.lpsm_mb:blocks.stairs=Stairs
guide.lpsm_mb:blocks.stairs.desc=§lStairs§r are blocks that allow mobs and players to change elevation without jumping.\n\n§lObtained:§r Crafted by placing 6 blocks in a stair like shape.\n\n§lVariants:§r GENERATED.\n
guide.lpsm_mb:blocks.stairs.sponge=§lSponge stairs§r are stair-shaped sponge blocks that absorb nearby water when placed. They only remove water within a 6 block radius.
guide.lpsm_mb:blocks.stairs.tnt=§lTNT stairs§r are stair-shaped TNT blocks that explode when ignited. They have a blast radius of 4 blocks.
guide.lpsm_mb:blocks.stairs.redstone_block=§lRedstone block stairs§r are stair-shaped redstone blocks that emit power to nearby blocks. They provide a redstone signal strength of 15.
##template: guide.lpsm_mb:blocks.slabs.desc=A §lslab§r is a half-height version of its respective block.\n\n§lObtained:§r Crafted by placing 3 blocks in a slab like shape.\n\n§lVariants:§r {{slabs}}.\n
guide.lpsm_mb:blocks.slabs=Slabs
guide.lpsm_mb:blocks.slabs.sponge=A §lsponge slab§r is a half-height version of a sponge that absorbs nearby water when placed. It removes water within a 3 block radius (or 6 if double).
guide.lpsm_mb:blocks.slabs.tnt=A §lTNT slab§r is a half-height TNT block that explode when ignited. They have a blast radius of 4 blocks.
guide.lpsm_mb:blocks.slabs.redstone_block=A §lRedstone block slab§r is a half-height redstone block that emit power to nearby blocks. They provide a redstone signal strength of 7 (or 15 if double).
##template: guide.lpsm_mb:blocks.layers.desc=§lLayer§r blocks are full blocks divided into up to 8 stackable layers that can be built up over time. Interacting while holding the same block adds more layers, increasing its height.\n\n§lObtained:§r Crafted by placing any block in the Stonecutter.\n\n§lVariants:§r {{layers}}.\n
guide.lpsm_mb:blocks.layers=Layers
guide.lpsm_mb:blocks.layers.sponge=§lSponge layers§r are stackable sponge layers that absorb nearby water when placed. They only remove water within a 0-6 block radius depending on the number of layers.
guide.lpsm_mb:blocks.layers.tnt=§lTNT layers§r are stackable TNT layers that explode when ignited. They have a blast radius of 4 blocks.
guide.lpsm_mb:blocks.layers.redstone_block=§lRedstone block layers§r are stackable redstone block that emit power to nearby blocks. They provide a redstone signal strength of 2, 4, 6, 8, 10, 12, 14, or 15 depending on the number of layers.
guide.lpsm_mb:blocks.vertical_slabs=Vertical Slabs
##template: guide.lpsm_mb:blocks.vertical_slabs.desc=A §lvertical slab§r is a half-width version of its respective block.\n\n§lObtained:§r Crafted by placing 3 blocks in a vertical slab like shape.\n\n§lVariants:§r {{vertical_slabs}}.\n
guide.lpsm_mb:blocks.vertical_slabs.sponge=A §lsponge vertical slab§r is a half-width version of a sponge that absorbs nearby water when placed. It removes water within a 3 block radius (or 6 if double).
guide.lpsm_mb:blocks.vertical_slabs.tnt=A §lTNT vertical slab§r is a half-width TNT block that explodes when ignited. It has a blast radius of 4 blocks.
guide.lpsm_mb:blocks.vertical_slabs.redstone_block=A §lRedstone block vertical slab§r is a half-width redstone block that emit power to nearby blocks. They provide a redstone signal strength of 7 (or 15 if double).
guide.lpsm_mb:items.guide_book.desc=A reference that explains new blocks, items, and mechanics added by this Add-On.\n\n§lStackable:§r No\n\n§lUsage:§r An interface to help you understand everything added by the Add-On.\n\n§lObtain:§r Crafted with a Oak Vertical Slab and Book.
guide.lpsm_mb:creator=Creator
guide.lpsm_mb:creator.desc=§lDiscord Server:§r\nJoin the community at §udiscord.lpsmods.dev§r for Add-On help, updates, and creator discussion.
guide.lpsm_mb:changelogs=Changelogs
guide.lpsm_mb:changelogs.v200=v2.0.0 §u[Installed]§r
guide.lpsm_mb:changelogs.v200.desc=- Requires Assets+ v2.0.1\n- Updated for Minecraft 26.20\n- Added compatibility with Vibrant Visuals.\n- Blocks can now be waterlogged.\n- Changed ids to §llpsm_mb§r\n- Added a guide book.
guide.lpsm_mb:changelogs.v170=v1.7.0
guide.lpsm_mb:changelogs.v170.desc=- Requires Assets+ v1.8.0\n- Updated for 1.21.50\n- Changed
guide.lpsm_mb:changelogs.v160=v1.6.0
guide.lpsm_mb:changelogs.v160.desc=- Requires Assets+ v1.7.0\n- Updated for 1.21.44\n- All blocks now use custom components. See docs for more info.\n- Merged with more stairs and slabs Add-On.\n- Most blocks should behave like their full block counter part. Submit a bug report if this is not the case.\n- Changed up stair hitboxes so you can use walls underneath to make a stair like hitbox.\n- Blocks from moress should get converted to moreblocks
guide.lpsm_mb:changelogs.v150=v1.5.0
guide.lpsm_mb:changelogs.v150.desc=- Updated for 1.20.51\n- Requires Assets+ v1.6.0\n- Added \"Update 1.21\" toggle in behavior pack settings.
guide.lpsm_mb:changelogs.v140=v1.4.0
guide.lpsm_mb:changelogs.v140.desc=- Updated for 1.20.41\n- Increasing layers will now play the sound for all players within 17 blocks.\n- You can now place the layers up side down.\n- Mangrove, Slime, and Honey layers have custom models.
guide.lpsm_mb:changelogs.v130=v1.3.0
guide.lpsm_mb:changelogs.v130.desc=- Updated for 1.19.80\n- Requres Assets Plus v1.4.0\n- Added all 1.20 blocks\n- You can now use a Stone Axe to unwax, and deoxidize copper
guide.lpsm_mb:changelogs.v121=v1.2.1
guide.lpsm_mb:changelogs.v121.desc=- The second layer should now use the proper geometry.\n- All glass side textures should use the custom texture to make the sides look better.
guide.lpsm_mb:changelogs.v120=v1.2.0
guide.lpsm_mb:changelogs.v120.desc=- Updated for 1.19\n- Now uses Assets Plus v1.2.0\n- Removed give functions. You can obtain all items through the creative menu.\n- Removed all crafting recipes. You can use the stonecutter instead.\n- Removed concrete shard item\n- Removed terracotta shard item\n- Removed yarn item\n- Added TONS of new layer blocks\n- All blocks can be obtained by placing the full block inside a stonecutter
guide.lpsm_mb:changelogs.v110=v1.1.0
guide.lpsm_mb:changelogs.v110.desc=- min Minecraft version ( 1.180 )\n- Blocks will now show up in the creative inventory.
guide.lpsm_mb:changelogs.v100=v1.0.0
guide.lpsm_mb:changelogs.v100.desc=- Initial release
